-- ============================================================================
-- PD8 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Well Intervention, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE WINDOWED READING AND WHAT IT DECIDES. Five of its
-- six graded fields come back from ONE `chanDiagnosis` call, and one of those
-- five IS THE WINDOW: the engine grades the start of the late window in days
-- alongside the two slopes and two fit qualities measured on it. The sixth is
-- `skinPiMultiplier` on a designed acid job, which is what the ALTERNATIVE to
-- a water job is worth. The seam is again in the code and not in a syllabus:
-- the Associate tier is every call that takes no window, this tier is the one
-- call that takes a window and the one call that prices the other treatment,
-- and the Expert tier is those same calls re-run at the edges.
--
-- THE TIER IS BUILT ON ONE SENTENCE. THE WINDOW THE LINE WAS TAKEN OVER IS
-- PART OF THE ANSWER. `lateFromT` is graded here for exactly that reason. It
-- is also the ONLY DIMENSIONAL NUMBER this module returns anywhere: the engine
-- is a diagnostic and it sizes nothing, so every other continuous return is a
-- slope, a fit quality, a span or a dimensionless group, and every verdict is
-- a string or a boolean and cannot be graded at all. A tier that reported the
-- slopes without the window would have reported half of a reading.
--
-- HOW THE WINDOW IS CHOSEN, AND IT IS NOT CHOSEN BY THE DATA. The cut index is
-- floor(n (1 - lateFraction)) and `lateFraction` defaults to 0.5. Nothing in
-- the module reads the history to place the cut, there is no guidance anywhere
-- on what to set it to, there is no sweep helper, and nothing in the return
-- object names its effect. The default 0.5 is also exactly the window the
-- oracle reads its four published histories on, series[n//2:], which is why
-- the published cases and the default agree and why that agreement proves
-- nothing about any other window. This tier owns reading a diagnosis AT a
-- stated window and saying so every time. The tier above owns what the dial is
-- worth in money.
--
-- WHAT THE VERDICT ACTUALLY TURNS ON, AND IT IS ONE COMPARISON. The mechanism
-- is decided by `derivativeSlope` against `coningSlope` -0.1 at one end and
-- `channellingSlope` 1.3 at the other, with everything between called ordinary
-- displacement, and `screenTreatments` then turns channelling into a water
-- shutoff CANDIDATE and displacement or coning into a BLOCK. So the whole
-- spend rests on one number against one round threshold, on a comparison the
-- module's own comment has already conceded cannot separate the two pictures
-- on a power law. This tier has to be able to name which threshold decided a
-- given verdict, and to say what `ambiguousBand` 0.25 does when the answer
-- lands near the line: it reports the closeness rather than resolving it, and
-- it forces `confidence` to low.
--
-- THREE THINGS THE TIER MUST NOT LET A LEARNER ASSUME.
--
--   THE TWO SLOPES IN ONE RETURN OBJECT WERE MEASURED ON DIFFERENT DATA.
--   `worSlope` is fitted over EVERY late sample. `derivativeSlope` is fitted
--   over only the late samples whose derivative is positive. On the teaching
--   well at the default window that is 19 samples against 15, the two come
--   back side by side as 1.040602176 and 1.442132492, a gap of 0.401530316,
--   and NOTHING in the object says they sit on different windows. Worse,
--   `spanDecades` describes the second window only while being named as though
--   it described the reading: on that same well it reports 0.900620470 for a
--   window that actually runs 1.157940604 log cycles, 0.257320134 of a log
--   cycle short. A learner who reads the two slopes as two views of one fit
--   has been misled by the shape of the return object, not by the arithmetic.
--
--   A DIAGNOSIS IS NOT A RECOMMENDATION, AND THE SCREENING READS LESS THAN THE
--   DIAGNOSIS OFFERS. `screenTreatments` takes the diagnosis and reads
--   `mechanism.id`. It reads `confidence` in EXACTLY ONE PLACE, the channelling
--   branch, where it appends a line about confirming with a production log. The
--   displacement and coning branches, which BLOCK, read neither the confidence
--   nor the ambiguous flag, so the caveat is attached to the verdict that
--   spends money and not to the one that refuses to. A learner has to be able
--   to say what the screening did with the answer and what it never looked at.
--
--   AND THE SENTENCE A PLANNER PASTES INTO A RECOMMENDATION IS WRONG ON THE
--   COMMONEST BRANCH. `screenTreatments` branches on `mechanism.id` alone and
--   pushes a fixed reason per branch: coning says the derivative is "falling",
--   channelling says "climbing", both right, and DISPLACEMENT SAYS "FLAT". But
--   displacement in this engine is the ROUGHLY PROPORTIONAL CLIMB, and
--   `chanDiagnosis` in the same file writes "climbing at a slope of 1.00, which
--   is about proportional" for the very same mechanism. On the published
--   displacement history the module therefore reports a derivative climbing at
--   a slope of exactly one and, one function later, calls that same derivative
--   flat in the reason text. The string is emitted on EVERY displacement well
--   and it is one of the two sentences that get pasted into a recommendation.
--   The module contradicts itself between two functions in one file, and this
--   tier owns it because this tier is where the screening is read.
--
-- WHAT THE ACID JOB IS DOING IN THIS TIER, AND IT IS NOT A DIGRESSION. The
-- water job and the stimulation are the two things the money can go to, and
-- only one of them depends on the classifier. `skinPiMultiplier` is a ratio of
-- two pseudo-steady-state groups and it is the second thing the oracle checks,
-- against a full SI Darcy rate, so it is the one number in this tier standing
-- on an independent published check. It is also EXACTLY 1 when the skin does
-- not change, to the last bit, because it is one number divided by itself. And
-- it is worth far more on a damaged well than a clean one: on the published
-- geometry one unit of skin removed from 20 is worth 3.717372 percent, and one
-- unit removed from 1 is worth 12.657067 percent. A learner who can say why
-- the same unit is worth three times as much has understood that the group
-- sits in a denominator.
--
-- WHAT THIS TIER MUST NOT PROMISE, AND IT IS HANDED STRAIGHT UPWARD. THE ONLY
-- PART OF THIS MODULE THAT RETURNS A VERDICT IS THE PART WITH NO GOLDEN. The
-- published file commits four labelled histories and a late derivative slope
-- for each, five skin pairs, one geometry floor and one power law, and it
-- publishes NO expected mechanism, NO expected confidence, NO expected verdict,
-- NO expected refusal and NO expected block reason. `chanDiagnosis`,
-- `screenTreatments`, `rankTreatments` and `skinFromPiRatio` are not asserted
-- against anything at all. This tier can state that as a limit honestly and
-- without any Expert material: every verdict a learner produces here is
-- produced by code that nothing is checking. Section 2 of the digest runs the
-- classifier over the four published histories and prints the four assertions
-- nobody wrote, and two of them deserve saying out loud. The coning history is
-- where the two estimators visibly separate in the second decimal on data with
-- no noise in it. And the displacement history comes back at HIGH confidence
-- and NOT flagged ambiguous on a slope of exactly one, which the oracle's own
-- docstring calls the case that genuinely needs the plot and a person.
--
-- SAY WHAT IT REFUSES, EVERY TIME. In a course about a classifier with no
-- golden the refusals are half the teaching, and every one is printed in the
-- digest with its exact words: fewer than six samples is refused outright, a
-- last-sample ratio below `minWor` 0.1 short-circuits the whole diagnosis, a
-- derivative fit spanning less than `minSpanDecades` 0.4 is refused, and a
-- derivative fit below `minR2` 0.5 is refused as noise. Which refusal fired,
-- and on what, is a real answer.
--
-- The only numbers that travel to the tier above are the well's own stated
-- history, its stated geometry and the stated window. The Expert tier restates
-- all of them and re-runs every call for itself.
-- ============================================================================

values ('intervention', 'intermediate', '{"modules":[{"key":"m01-the-late-window","title":"The Late Window","lesson_keys":["l01-why-the-reading-is-late","l02-the-window-as-a-fraction","l03-where-the-window-starts","l04-the-dial-is-clamped","l05-what-a-window-assumes"]},{"key":"m02-the-diagnosis","title":"The Diagnosis","lesson_keys":["l01-two-fits-from-one-call","l02-the-derivative-slope-decides","l03-the-ambiguous-band","l04-how-confidence-is-assigned","l05-what-the-verdict-rests-on"]},{"key":"m03-what-removing-skin-is-worth","title":"What Removing Skin Is Worth","lesson_keys":["l01-a-ratio-of-two-groups","l02-what-a-stimulation-buys","l03-auditing-a-claimed-uplift","l04-what-the-multiplier-refuses"]},{"key":"m04-the-water-gate","title":"The Water Gate","lesson_keys":["l01-seven-treatments-one-well","l02-the-water-cut-gate","l03-the-mechanism-gate","l04-blocked-against-no","l05-what-a-block-reason-says"]},{"key":"m05-the-gas-side","title":"The Gas Side","lesson_keys":["l01-the-gas-oil-ratio-gate","l02-measured-against-an-expectation","l03-the-instruction-it-ends-on","l04-what-the-screening-never-checks"]},{"key":"m06-the-professional-reading","title":"The Professional Reading","lesson_keys":["l01-the-story-so-far","l02-working-the-capstone","l03-onward"]}]}'::jsonb, 1)
on conflict (app_slug, tier) do update
  set structure = excluded.structure,
      content_version = excluded.content_version,
      active = true,
      updated_at = now();

delete from public.academy_quiz_questions
 where app_slug = 'intervention' and tier = 'intermediate';

